  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nI looked into reverting https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11656 as the CSS-side change did not work out and it seems @tabatkins has forgotten about it, but I don't really understand what's involved.\n\nIn particular for the [corresponding WPT changes](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/55116) it seems @bfgeek removed some of the test changes in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/2f10d7c0766d34396b0d47842d435c0df146d2eb but `html/semantics/popovers/popover-alignment-001.html`and `html/semantics/popovers/popover-alignment-002.html` are still there, were modified by @fantasai, and have multiple passing implementations. If we revert the specification change, what does that mean for popover-alignment-001 and 2?\n\ncc @whatwg/css ",
